# Scheduling / optimization
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Goal:
#   - Improve instruction-level parallelism (ILP) in the inner j-loop.
#   - Keep the original data access pattern: row-major over L[i, j] and
#     sequential access over x[j].
#
# Strategy:
#   1. Strip-mine (divide) the inner j-loop into an outer "block" loop jo and
#      an inner fixed-size loop ji of width 4:
#         for j in 0..i-1
#       -->
#         for jo in 0..i/4-1
#           for ji in 0..3
#             j = 4*jo + ji
#           # tail loop for remaining iterations
#
#      This preserves the original loop order and dependencies but exposes a
#      small fixed-size inner loop.
#
#   2. Unroll the fixed-size inner ji loop (factor 4). This lets the C
#      compiler more easily keep x[i] in a register and schedule the
#      multiply-subtract operations efficiently, without changing any data
#      dependencies or memory access patterns.
#
#   3. Run simplify() to clean up algebraic artifacts from the transforms.
#
# All transformations are performed with Exo scheduling primitives, which
# preserve functional equivalence of the kernel.

kernel_trisolv_sched = kernel_trisolv

# 1. Strip-mine the inner j loop by a factor of 4.
j_loop = kernel_trisolv_sched.find_loop("j")
kernel_trisolv_sched = divide_loop(
    kernel_trisolv_sched,
    j_loop,
    4,                 # block size in j
    ("jo", "ji"),      # new loop indices: outer and inner
    tail="cut",        # generate a separate tail loop for the remainder
)

# 2. Unroll the fixed-size inner ji loop in the main strip-mined part.
#    After divide_loop, there are two ji loops; the first one has a constant
#    bound (4) and is the one we want to unroll.
ji_loop = kernel_trisolv_sched.find_loop("ji")
kernel_trisolv_sched = unroll_loop(kernel_trisolv_sched, ji_loop)

# 3. Simplify resulting expressions and clean up the IR.
kernel_trisolv_sched = simplify(kernel_trisolv_sched)

# Export the scheduled version under the original name expected by the C code.
kernel_trisolv = kernel_trisolv_sched
EXO END
